  "result": "I opened the issue: **https://github.com/acme/textstats/issues/13**. I didn't change any code.\n\n**Please check it went to the right repo.** In this checkout, `origin` points to a local folder (`/tmp/model-router-bench-k8vke5v_/origin.git`), not GitHub. The issue was filed on `acme/textstats` because that's the GitHub repo `gh` picked when run from this directory, under the account `bench-user`. Nothing in the git setup confirms it's the project you meant. If it's wrong, you can close #13 and I'll file it somewhere else.\n\n**What the issue says:**\n- **Bug:** `word_count` in `textstats/__init__.py:4` uses `len(text.split(\" \"))`. `\"\".split(\" \")` returns `[\"\"]`, so an empty string counts as 1 word.\n- **Same cause, other wrong results:** `\"   \"` gives 4, `\"a  b\"` gives 3, and `\"a\\nb\"` gives 1.\n- **Suggested fix:** use `len(text.split())`, which is how `average_word_length` in the same file already splits words, and add tests for these inputs.",
